# `npm run guide` prints a guide to stdout, and npm prints its own `> patchscore@0.1.0 guide`
# banner to stdout too — so `npm run guide -- … > guide.md` produced a file with two lines of
# npm in front of §8's first heading. `--silent` on every invocation is a footgun (the one time
# it is forgotten is the time the bytes are wrong), so it is set here once for the project.
#
# This silences npm's own logging, not the scripts': a failing `npm run verify` still prints
# every line vitest and tsc wrote, and still exits nonzero. What goes is the run banner and
# npm's `ERR!` epilogue, neither of which carries information the underlying tool did not
# already give.
loglevel=silent
